 '[{"text":"Must lie on one of the particles","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Represents the average position of the mass distribution of the system","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Is always at the geometric center of the container","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Moves independently of any external force","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'The center of mass represents the average (mass-weighted) position of a system of particles, and its motion is governed by the net external force on the system.'),
('NEET UG', 'Physics', 'Mechanics', 'easy', 'mcq',
 'Torque is best defined as the:',
 '[{"text":"Turning effect of a force about an axis (moment of force)","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Total kinetic energy of a rotating body","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Rate of change of linear momentum","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Force acting along the axis of rotation","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Torque is the rotational analogue of force, measuring the turning effect a force produces about a chosen axis or pivot point.'),

